      "writtenOn": "2026-06-29T16:32:45Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Hi Joakim,\n\nThanks for the excellent feedback on this. Really appreciate you taking time and helping me to make this change better. I will change the commit message to indicate the model numbers clearly.\n\nRegarding the separating them, I feel that it should be okay to have both here. This change is in port-mapping, where we are adding the enum for 13.1.1 and 17.1.0. OpenROADM model support is already there in TPCE/models.\n\nHaving both together makes it convenient, because we use the latest model revision number in port-mapping (for instance 17.1.0 revision dates will be used).\n\nIf I have to separate them, then we again have to change the revision dates in port-mapping YANG file, corresponding to reflect 17.1.0. \n\nKindly let me know what you think!",
